# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# Nothing here is required — the pipeline runs with no `.env` at all.

# Optional path overrides, if the export lives outside the project directory.
# SPOTIFY_EXPORT_DIR=/path/to/Spotify Extended Streaming History
# SPOTIFY_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data
# SPOTIFY_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/.cache
# SPOTIFY_OUTPUT_DIR=/path/to/output

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spotify Web API credentials are NO LONGER USED.
#
# The design called for Spotify's artist endpoint as a genre fallback, because
# it used to return a `genres` array. It does not any more: /v1/artists/{id}
# now answers 200 with `genres`, `popularity` and `followers` all absent
# (checked against Drake, Taylor Swift, Metallica and ArrDee), batch
# /v1/artists and /top-tracks answer 403, and search never carried genres.
#
# Untagged artists are backfilled from MusicBrainz release-group tags instead,
# which needs no credentials. Nothing reads SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID or
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET — you can delete the developer app.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
